      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "Three groves marked for cutting. The soldiers say we killed their woodcutters."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Then take the groves back. Leave their fort alone; we need the cutting stopped, not another graveyard."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Captain Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "You want us gone? Prove those roots hide something other than your own crimes."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "All three groves are ours again. The cutters have put down their axes."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Captain Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "After what has happened here, I will not call us friends. But I will hear what you know about the missing woodcutters."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Come to the central grove under a truce. Lark can wake the roots and show us what they remember."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "Dain is gone. We can still stop the cutting and find out what happened to the woodcutters."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The three groves are ours, but Dain will never see what lies beneath them."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "His death will not bring back the woodcutters. Tamsin asked to hear the roots; let her come under a truce."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "Tools, not trophies. Leave them where their owners will find them. There are six coins tucked in the handle; we can use those for the vigil."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "They call the trees an obstacle. They have marked three groves for cutting."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Then we stand where their marks are. No chase into their fort. We need our roots back, not their bones."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The wolves know the narrow paths. Their hunters know where to point a spear. Let the boars go first when the woods run out."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Captain Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "We came for timber. Something in the old grove has been killing our woodcutters. Was that you?"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "No. Come back at dusk, with empty hands, and I will show you what wakes beneath the stones."
    }
  ]
}
